WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.443
Local processing can keep images and outputs under direct control, but deployment still needs a data policy.

00:00:08.443 --> 00:00:12.779
Define storage, retention, access, export, logs, and deletion.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:19.397
Avoid sending images to external services unless that flow is approved and transparent.

00:00:19.397 --> 00:00:26.015
Review the model and runtime licenses for the intended use, distribution, and modification.

00:00:26.015 --> 00:00:31.263
Track model source, file integrity, version, prompt template, and dependencies.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:36.055
Treat model updates as software changes with regression testing.

00:00:36.055 --> 00:00:41.760
Operational workflows need queues, timeouts, retries, alert routing, and human review.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:53.398
A fallback model or simpler pipeline can preserve service when the preferred model exceeds memory or fails, but the system should label changed capability.

00:00:53.398 --> 00:00:58.647
Cost includes hardware, power, cooling, storage, administration, and reviewer time.

00:00:58.647 --> 00:01:04.352
A larger model may cost more operationally without improving the task.

00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:10.513
Monitor throughput, completion, latency, memory pressure, temperature, queue depth, and output quality.

00:01:10.513 --> 00:01:13.936
Do not blindly trust model output.

00:01:13.936 --> 00:01:19.641
Important decisions should link back to visible evidence and accountable review.

00:01:19.641 --> 00:01:29.454
Local vision systems should not be used for covert stalking, harassment, inappropriate surveillance, or identifying private individuals without lawful authority.

00:01:29.454 --> 00:01:36.071
Reevaluate over time as cameras, documents, use cases, models, drivers, and runtimes change.

00:01:36.071 --> 00:01:39.951
Keep a known-good configuration and rollback path.

00:01:39.951 --> 00:01:47.938
Deployment success means stable, privacy-conscious assistance that remains understandable when the model is wrong or unavailable.
